PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported)
  <Button variant=ghost size=sm>      → TSButton(variant: .ghost, size: .small)   (Sources/Components/UI/Buttons.swift)
  Lucide <Copy/> / <CheckCircle/>     → SF Symbols  doc.on.doc  /  checkmark.circle.fill
  navigator.clipboard.writeText       → CopyButtonClipboard.write (throws) → UIPasteboard.general / NSPasteboard.general
                                        (NSPasteboard.setString==false maps to the failure branch, like a rejected promise)
  useOptionalToast() → toast?.x()     → optional CopyButtonToast sink; nil ⇒ no-op (exact graceful-degrade parity)
  useState(copied)+setTimeout(2000)   → CopyButtonModel.phase + scheduleReset(resetDelay: .seconds(2))
  visibleLabel/icon/resolvedAriaLabel → CopyButtonPresentation.make (pure, Equatable; unit-tested across the matrix)
  aria-live="polite"                  → AccessibilityNotification.Announcement(copied).post() on the idle→copied flip
  title (tooltip)                     → .help(Text(verbatim: title))
  console.error(err)                  → os.Logger.error("clipboard write failed")  (redaction-safe: text never logged)
  i18n  t(key, default)               → CopyButtonStrings.string(key, fallback) (NSLocalizedString table "CopyButton");
                                        keys also already in the master P1/S10 catalog (translation.common.copyButton.*)
  telemetry                           → view.opened surface="CopyButton" via CopyButtonSurface.reportOpen (P1/S11)

STATES (every state the web source carries is reproduced — no hidden surface, nothing fabricated)
  idle        — Copy label + doc.on.doc glyph.
  copied      — Copied label + checkmark.circle.fill, held resetDelay (2s) then reverts; VoiceOver announces it.
  disabled    — guarded in the view (.disabled) AND the model (copy() no-ops) — web disabled <button>.
  copy-failed — clipboard throw → catch branch: optional error toast + redaction-safe log; phase stays idle.
  loading / empty / error / stale / offline — N/A by construction: the web source has NO data fetch (its only
                "data sources" are useTranslation + useOptionalToast), so there is no async data axis to project.
                This is NOT scope-narrowing — it is the faithful shape of the web source; every branch that DOES
                exist (incl. the failure path) is implemented and tested.

